OLD_SECTION (line 13)
**It owns the inside of the element you give it.** On each run it appends a `<span class="vAutoWriter">` to your target (reusing one if it is already there) and types into that span, not into the target directly. When `config.showCursor` is on, a second `<span class="vAutoWriterBlinker">` follows it as the caret. Your target element should therefore be an empty container [em dash] anything already inside it sits alongside the typed text, and the span is emptied at the start of every run.
